# 🌟 **UNITY ANIMATION MINDMAP (TEXT VISUAL)**

Use this as your *mental blueprint* forever.

```
──────────────────────────────────────────────
       🎬 UNITY ANIMATION MASTER BLUEPRINT
──────────────────────────────────────────────

              ┌──────────────────────────┐
              │  1. TIME SYSTEM          │
              └──────────────────────────┘
                  • Time.deltaTime
                  • t += Time.deltaTime
                  • progress = t / duration   (0 → 1)
                  
                  ► TIME is the heartbeat of animation


              ┌──────────────────────────┐
              │  2. VALUES (START/END)   │
              └──────────────────────────┘
                  • startValue
                  • endValue
                  • currentValue

                  Examples:
                  - startScale = localScale
                  - endScale = startScale * 1.5
                  - startAlpha = 0
                  - endAlpha   = 1

                  ► No animation is possible without start & end


              ┌──────────────────────────┐
              │  3. SMOOTH FUNCTIONS     │
              └──────────────────────────┘
                  • Lerp()        → linear smooth
                  • SmoothDamp()  → spring/eased smooth
                  • MoveTowards() → constant speed

                  ► Choose SMOOTH CURVE type (feel of motion)


              ┌──────────────────────────┐
              │  4. COROUTINE ENGINE     │
              └──────────────────────────┘
                  while (t < duration)
                  {
                      t += deltaTime
                      progress = t/duration
                      value = Lerp(start, end, progress)
                      yield return null
                  }

                  ► This loop is the engine of ALL animations


              ┌──────────────────────────┐
              │  5. UPDATE vs COROUTINE  │
              └──────────────────────────┘
                  • Update() → continuous logic
                  • Coroutine → timed animations

                  ► Anything with a duration → Coroutine


              ┌──────────────────────────┐
              │  6. APPLY THE VALUE      │
              └──────────────────────────┘
                  Examples:
                  • transform.localScale = value
                  • mat.color = value
                  • transform.position = value
                  • uiCanvasGroup.alpha = value

                  ► The animated value MUST be applied each frame


──────────────────────────────────────────────
           💎 ONE TEMPLATE TO RULE THEM ALL
──────────────────────────────────────────────

float t = 0;

while (t < duration)
{
    t += Time.deltaTime;          // time rising
    float p = t / duration;       // 0 → 1

    current = Lerp(start, end, p);  // animation
    (apply current value)           // scale/color/move...

    yield return null;             // wait next frame
}

──────────────────────────────────────────────
```

🔥 **If this template is clear → you can animate ANYTHING in Unity.**

